<sn><md>### Remote Name vs Remote Path

This distinction is important.

Suppose you have:

```text
gdrive:Study/Physics
```

It consists of:

```text
gdrive
  │
  └── Remote name

Study/Physics
  │
  └── Remote path
```

So:

| Part                 | Example                | Meaning                                |
| -------------------- | ---------------------- | -------------------------------------- |
| Remote name          | `gdrive`               | Name you gave the Rclone configuration |
| Remote path          | `Study/Physics`        | Location inside that remote            |
| Complete remote path | `gdrive:Study/Physics` | Remote + path                          |

</md></sn><sn><md>### The Same Command Can Work With Different Remotes

For example:

```bash
rclone copy Documents gdrive:Documents
```

Google Drive.

```bash
rclone copy Documents onedrive:Documents
```

OneDrive.

```bash
rclone copy Documents s3:mybucket/Documents
```

S3.

The **local source stays the same**, while the remote destination changes.
</md></sn>